                <pb facs="pm_d27-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d27-1"/>

                <head>PM–27. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 28, 1959, mobs of demonstrators again attempted to enter the Panama
                    Canal Zone. Prevented from entering this area by the Panamanian National Guard,
                    the rioters proceeded to the business district in Panama City where they smashed
                    windows and looted American commercial establishments. Twelve American soldiers
                    and eighteen Panamanians—National Guardsmen and civilians—received treatment <pb
                        facs="1017" n="929" type="typeset" xml:id="pg929"/> for injuries caused by
                    stone-throwing and tear-gas burns; at least 150 persons were arrested.
                    Documentation on these incidents is found in decimal files 611.19 and 719.00,
                    and also in ARA/OAP Files, Lot 64 D 67.</p>
            </div>
